            "review_title": "Review at Cachette Cafe",
            "review_text": "Jason T\n4 contributions\n1\nhidden gem: tea, chill electronica, cats, and a tattoo parlor\nJul 2016 • Solo\nThis place is not the easiest to find, and has a character all to its own. They make some interesting cocktails, serve the usual battery of coffees, and serve some great cinnamon tea. You take your shoes off before entering, and the music is generally chill electronica played quite loudly, combining for a cool vibe. The staff are incredibly friendly, as are the cats. There's a tattoo parlor up in the loft, and a cozy balcony overlooking Hang Bac street. For me, it's a great place to take my laptop and work; I can pace around barefoot bobbing my head, and nobody cares.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nWritten August 1, 2016",
